The preceding <Dynkin diagram> identifies the root system $D_3$ with $A_3$. The classification of finite-dimensional complex <simple Lie algebras> by connected Dynkin diagrams therefore gives
$$
\boxed{\mathfrak{so}_6(\mathbb C)\cong\mathfrak{sl}_4(\mathbb C)}.
$$
This is the <isomorphism between so6 and sl4>. Both algebras have dimension $15$, consistently with the classification.

